    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n34293" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pĕcŭīnus</span></b> , a,
			um, adj.
		pecu. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>, <i>of cattle</i> (ante-
			and post-class.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">daps,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cato, R. R. 132, 2</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ossa,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">App. M. 8, p. 215, 49</span></i>
			.— <b>
				<i>Absol.</i>
			</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pecuina et ferina,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">App. M. 11 <i>init.</i></span></i>
			 —</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>, <i>beastly</i>, <i>brutal</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">animus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">App. Mag. 281, 11</span></i>
			.</div>
